.TH PEISO 1 2026-10-21 "Peios peiso 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
peiso \- build bootable Peios ISOs from ppk packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B peiso build
.RB [ \-\-mkirf
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-mkuki
.IR file ]
.B \-\-out
.I file spec
.br
.B peiso
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help | \-V | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B peiso
builds an ISO that boots a Peios live system under UEFI, from the
packages a spec names.
.PP
It finds each package in the spec's repositories and copies every one
into the ISO's own store, checking each as
.BR ppk (1)
fetches it.
It composes the initramfs from the packages the spec puts there and those
of the live system, with prelude as its init, writes the live system's
environment profile into it as
.IR /system/live.toml ,
and packs it with
.BR mkirf .
.B mkuki
then makes the initramfs, the kernel and its command line into a unified
kernel image, which
.B peiso
places as the loader of an EFI system partition image.
The ISO holds that image, as its UEFI boot image, and the store, at
.IR /artifacts .
.PP
At boot, prelude runs the live-root hook, which composes the live system
from the profile and the packages in the initramfs's own store, on a
tmpfs.
.SH THE SPEC
A spec is a TOML file.
Paths in it are relative to its directory.
.PP
.RS
.EX
disable_default_repos = true

[[repository]]
filepath = "../pkgs/_artifacts"

[kernel]
file = "vmlinuz"
cmdline = "console=ttyS0 rd.shell"

[[package]]
name = "net.busybox.busybox"

[[package]]
name = "dev.peios.prelude"
liveboot = false
initramfs = true
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B disable_default_repos
Whether to leave out the default repository, pkgs.peios.org.
It is not available yet, so this must be
.BR true .
.TP
.B [[repository]]
A place packages come from:
.B filepath
names an artifact directory.
Repositories are searched in the order given, and must agree on what each
version of a package is.
.TP
.B [kernel]
The kernel the ISO boots:
.BR file ,
and its command line,
.BR cmdline ,
empty by default.
.TP
.B [[package]]
A package the ISO carries:
.B name
and
.BR version .
Without a version, the repositories together must hold one version of the
package for the host's architecture, since versions have no order to pick
the newest by.
.B liveboot
puts the package in the live system, and is
.B true
by default.
.B initramfs
puts it in the initramfs, and is
.B false
by default.
A package that is in neither is carried in the ISO's store only, for
fetching from later.
.TP
.B [initramfs]
What the initramfs holds outside
.IR usr ,
as an environment profile's
.B symlinks
and
.B dirs
give it.
By default
.I init
links to
.IR usr/sbin/prelude ,
with empty
.IR proc ,
.IR sys ,
and
.IR tmp .
A table given replaces the default.
.TP
.B [liveboot]
What the live system holds outside
.IR usr ,
in the same way.
By default
.I bin
and
.I sbin
link to
.I usr/bin
and
.IR usr/sbin ,
with an empty
.IR tmp .
.PP
Some keys are understood but refused until what they need exists:
.B edition
and
.B edition_package
until packages can depend on others,
.B url
in a repository until repositories on the network, and
.B autoinstall
and
.B offerinstall
until an installer.
Any other key is an error.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI build " spec"
Build the ISO
.I spec
describes and print its path.
It is built in a directory beside it, which is removed afterwards, and
renamed into place whole.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-out " file"
Write the ISO to
.IR file ,
replacing any there.
Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-mkirf " file"
Pack the initramfs with this
.BR mkirf ,
rather than the one on
.BR PATH .
.TP
.BI \-\-mkuki " file"
Make the unified kernel image with this
.BR mkuki ,
rather than the one on
.BR PATH .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including printing help or the version.
.TP
.B 1
Failure, such as a spec with errors, a package in no repository or with
several versions, a package that fails its checks, or a tool that fails.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: an unknown option or a missing argument.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B peiso
runs
.BR mkfs.vfat ,
.BR mmd ,
.BR mcopy ,
and
.B xorriso
from
.BR PATH .
None needs privilege.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ppk (1),
.BR pekit (1),
.BR mkirf (1),
.BR mkuki (1)
